<title>SPAIN: Popular H1 net attributable rises 4.2 pct.</title>
<headline>Popular H1 net attributable rises 4.2 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results for Banco Popular for the first six months through end June.</p>
<p>(billion pesetas, unless stated)</p>
<p> Net attributable profit		 31.41  vs  30.13</p>
<p> Net profit				  33.91  vs  32.25</p>
<p> Pretax profit			     51.57  vs  48.02</p>
<p> Net interest income		     86.75  vs  89.35</p>
<p>Return on assets (percent)	    1.95  vs   1.92</p>
<p>Return on equity (percent)	   20.57  vs  20.27</p>
<p>Ordinary income			118.88    vs  116.65</p>
<p>Operating income			61.17    vs   60.54</p>
<p>Interest revenue		     139.92    vs  163.68</p>
<p>Interest expenses		     53.92    vs   75.52</p>
<p>Equity portfolio yield		 0.76    vs    1.19</p>
<p>Fees and commissions		  27.19    vs   22.84</p>
<p>Financial/trading income	     4.94    vs    4.46</p>
<p>Operating costs			 50.23    vs   48.22</p>
<p>-personnel costs			37.29    vs   36.43</p>
<p>-general, administrative costs    11.02    vs   10.11</p>
<p>Depreciation			     4.51    vs    3.79</p>
<p>Other operating revenue		0.09    vs    0.06 Other</p>
<p>operating costs 3.07 vs 4.17</p>
<p>Net loss from</p>
<p>  equity-accounted holdings	  0.06    vs    0.26</p>
<p>Amortisation of goodwill	     0.05    vs    0.03</p>
<p>Gains on group transactions	  0.15    vs    0.02</p>
<p>Net loan-loss provisions	     6.70    vs    8.53</p>
<p>Net extraordinary losses	     2.94    vs    3.71</p>
<p>Corporate income tax		  17.66    vs   15.77</p>
<p>-- Madrid Newsroom +34 1 585 2167</p>
